1
00:05:32,000 --> 00:05:38,000
The Swan Princess Christmas is a family, animation,
fantasy film directed by Richard Rich.

2
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Princess Odette, Prince Derek and their trusted woodland friends reunite in this
all-new adventure for their first Christmas celebration together!

3
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:42,000
As the kingdom prepares for a festive holiday, the
villainous Rothbart plots to destroy Christmas.

4
00:22:08,000 --> 00:22:14,000
Will the castle friends be able to stop Rothbart and save the day?

5
00:27:40,000 --> 00:27:46,000
Told in beautiful CG animation for the very first time and featuring music by Anna Graceman from TV’s America’s Got
Talent, The Swan Princess Christmas is an enchanting musical holiday treat the whole family will enjoy!

6
00:33:12,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Prince Derek (voice), played by Yuri Lowenthal.

7
00:38:44,000 --> 00:38:50,000
Ferdinand the Chef (voice), played by Brian Nissen.

8
00:44:16,000 --> 00:44:22,000
Maid (voice), played by Catherine Parks.

9
00:49:48,000 --> 00:49:54,000
Number 9 / Footman (voice), played by David Lodge.

10
00:55:20,000 --> 00:55:26,000
Lord Rogers (voice), played by Joseph Medrano.

11
01:00:52,000 --> 01:00:58,000
Chamberlain (voice), played by James Arrington.

12
01:06:24,000 --> 01:06:30,000
The Swan Princess is an animated film series that began with the 1994 film The Swan
Princess, loosely based on the 1877 ballet Swan Lake by Pyotr Ilyich Tchaikovsky.

13
01:11:56,000 --> 01:12:02,000
There are twelve films in the series.

14
01:17:28,000 --> 01:17:34,000
The film explores themes of princess, kingdom, holiday, musical, sequel.
